findings.evidence:
From left to right along the far wall:
- a light-blue door with a barred lower panel, right next to the white block on the left, a little lower (on steps);
- a blue louvred window with no hood;
- a larger blue louvred window with a red hood;
- plain white wall up to the corner of the east range.
A tiled dado and a painted inscription line run below the windows. | model: One 'Entrance circuit blue barred window' with a red hood at x 49.0, and the 'closed blue service door' at x 50.92, to the right of the window.
